  "post": {
    "caption": "Andy Warhol never wound his Cartier. Warhol often wore a Cartier Tank watch, and he never wound it. He is quoted as saying a Tank is not for telling time, and that he wore it because it is the watch to wear. Louis Cartier made the first Tank in 1917: a rectangle in a world of round watches, with a Roman numeral dial, blued steel hands and a sapphire on the crown. Princess Diana was often seen in one, and a cheaper Tank arrived in the late 1970s.",
